You have a list of N user IDs and must find duplicates. A junior developer proposes the following solution:

```python
def find_duplicates(ids):
    dups = []
    for i in range(len(ids)):
        for j in range(i + 1, len(ids)):
            if ids[i] == ids[j] and ids[i] not in dups:
                dups.append(ids[i])
    return dups
```

Analyse the time complexity of this solution. Then propose an optimised version with O(n) complexity. Explain why your solution is more efficient.
